 the spec describes.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"+3.3V\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"REG2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"OUT\\\") (pintype \\\"unspecified\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"2\\\") (name \\\"+3V3\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs\"}], \"impact\": \"If the two labels are truly not joined, the MCUs and the I2C pull-ups would have no supply and the board would not boot. The likely cause is a labelling error, but the board would be non-functional as drawn.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The most concrete deviation is the PCA9685 A0 strap tied to +3.3V, which moves its I2C address away from the 0x40 stated in the spec. A second, lower-confidence concern is that the '+3V3' rail feeding the MCUs and pull-ups has no source, because the regulator output is on a separately named '+3.3V' net.\"}",
